  "body": "Follow-up closing the empirical validation gate condition from memos/2026-05-22-1430--thingalog-strategist--orgdef-strategist--oagp-adoption-cycle-pattern-promotion.openthing. The bootstrap skill (from skills/oagp-bootstrap/SKILL.md in the Thingalog repo) ran end-to-end against a real existing project (DangerStorm, ~130-build active SaaS) via a forked test environment per the org-state-fork pattern. All 5 phases (Survey → Propose → Ratify → Instantiate → Hand-off) executed cleanly with discipline preserved throughout: no auto-staffing, confidence-marker discipline in the proposal, explicit PO ratification gates at every phase boundary, preserve-don't-overwrite respected (existing memory/ folder + 11KB CLAUDE.md both preserved), bounded-authority on push (gracefully handled the no-remote test-fork case). Five SKILL.md iterations surfaced and were made (gitkeep for empty substrate folders; no-remote handling explicit; opening-sentence parameterization documented; canonical-reference-excludes-transcripts/ clause added; bootstrap-session transcript-position-tagging convention proposed). The pair (bootstrap + onboard) is now empirically validated on BOTH sides — onboard via /oagp-onboard-thingalog C4C shortcut (this morning, ~13:00 EDT); bootstrap via dangerstorm-oagp-test (this afternoon, 14:00-15:00 EDT). Cross-vendor cross-runtime adoption-cycle property is now empirically grounded, not just architecturally drafted. Recommendation: canonical promotion proceeds. One OAGP-spec-level question surfaced worth flagging (transcript position-tagging during bootstrap sessions — see §5 of body). Full validation record + the SKILL.md iterations + commit SHAs + transcript artifact pointer all in body_ref.",
